\newlabel{effect-of-defects-on-the-14mathrmc-cce-thickness-relation}{{}{6}{\texorpdfstring {3.3 Effect of defects on the \(^{14}\mathrm {C}\) CCE-thickness relation}{3.3 Effect of defects on the \^{}\{14\}\textbackslash mathrm\{C\} CCE-thickness relation}}{section*.17}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Fig.7. CCE curves under the \(^{14}\mathrm {C}\) continuous spectrum as a function of i-region thickness, with trap density \(N_t\) as the parameter. In the ideal model, CCE approaches saturation as thickness increases; at high defect density, trapping loss in the thick region is enhanced and CCE becomes nonmonotonic.}}{6}{figure.caption.18}\protected@file@percent }
